# why: A plugin can mark specific READ-ONLY calls of its own tools parallel-safe (a predicate on the call's arguments), so a tool whose reads and writes share one name admits its reads only. Inert until a plugin registers; HERMES_PLUGIN_PARALLEL_SAFE=0 switches it off.
